          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "The Cauchy slice $i_{\\max}(\\Sigma)$ in the development from step 2.1 and\nits complete flow from [F9] provide the product map used in [F8]. Pull the\ninitial local connection data [A2] to that product and use [F7] to construct\nits reference connection with curvature $\\bar F$ restricting to $\\beta_b$.\nSince $F_{\\max}$ is closed by [F3] and agrees with $\\bar F$ on the initial\nslice, [F8] gives a global one-form $\\alpha$ with\n$F_{\\max}-\\bar F=d\\alpha$. Adding $\\alpha/\\kappa_0$ to the normalized local\nconnection forms retains their transition maps and changes the physical\ncurvature by $\\kappa_0d(\\alpha/\\kappa_0)=d\\alpha$, giving $F_{\\max}$. Thus\nthe maximal field-strength development is realized in the supplied initial\nbundle sector.",
